---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const title = `Resources | Pinto Injury Resources`;
const description =
  'Plain-English California personal injury resources for Ontario, Upland, and Rancho Cucamonga. Learn the insurance process and what to do after an injury.';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
  </head>

  <body>
    <Header />

    <main class="container" style="padding: 3rem 1rem;">
      <header style="max-width: 70ch;">
        <h1 style="font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
          Injury Resources
        </h1>
        <p style="font-size: 1.125rem; opacity: 0.9; margin: 0;">
          Clear, practical general information about the insurance claim process in California—written for injured people in Ontario, Upland, and Rancho Cucamonga.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Start here</h2>

        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem;">
          <a class="card" href="/resources/what-to-do-after-a-car-accident-california">
  <h3>What to do after a car accident in California</h3>
  <p>A calm checklist for the first 24 hours and the first week.</p>
</a>

<a
  class="card"
  href="/resources/talking-to-insurance-adjusters-after-a-car-accident-common-mistakes"
>
  <h3>Talking to Insurance Adjusters After a Car Accident: Common Mistakes</h3>
  <p>
    Why insurance adjusters often call quickly, how recorded statements work,
    and common misunderstandings people have after a California car accident.
  </p>
</a>

<a class="card" href="/resources/how-insurance-companies-review-car-accident-claims-california">
  <h3>How insurance companies review car accident claims</h3>
  <p>Fault, evidence, statements, timelines, and why the process can feel slow.</p>
</a>
<a class="card" href="/resources/why-minor-car-accidents-can-lead-to-serious-injury-claims">
  <h3>Why minor car accidents can still lead to serious injury claims</h3>
  <p>How delayed symptoms, soft-tissue injuries, and concussions can develop after low-damage crashes.</p>
</a>
<a class="card" href="/resources/what-happens-when-fault-is-disputed-california">
  <h3>What happens when fault is disputed after a car accident</h3>
  <p>How comparative fault works, why insurers assign blame, and why disputes slow claims.</p>
</a>

<a class="card" href="/resources/how-long-car-accident-claims-usually-take-california">
  <h3>How long car accident claims usually take in California</h3>
  <p>Typical timelines, why delays happen, and how medical treatment and settlement sequencing affect timing.</p>
</a>
<a class="card" href="/resources/when-car-accident-claims-are-resolved-without-a-lawsuit-california">
  <h3>When car accident claims are resolved without a lawsuit</h3>
  <p>How pre-litigation resolution works, why many claims settle, what affects timing, and why lawsuits aren’t automatic.</p>
</a>
<a
  class="card"
  href="/resources/why-early-settlement-offers-after-car-accidents-are-often-incomplete-california"
>
  <h3>Why early settlement offers after car accidents are often incomplete</h3>
  <p>
    Why fast offers exist, how releases work, what future treatment unknowns can look like, and how pressure can show up early in the process.
  </p>
</a>
<a
  class="card"
  href="/resources/medical-treatment-documentation-car-accident-california"
>
  <h3>Medical treatment and documentation after a car accident</h3>
  <p>
    How insurers typically review medical records, why timelines and follow-ups receive attention, what gaps in care can signal during claim evaluation, and how documentation helps establish the progression of an injury.
  </p>
</a>
<a
  class="card"
  href="/resources/why-documentation-matters-after-a-car-accident-california"
>
  <h3>Why documentation matters after a car accident</h3>
  <p>
    How insurers build a claim file, what types of records are commonly reviewed (police reports, photos, estimates), and why missing or delayed documents can slow the process.
  </p>
</a>

<a
  class="card"
  href="/resources/why-insurance-companies-ask-for-so-much-evidence-after-car-accident-california"
>
  <h3>Why insurance companies ask for so much evidence after a car accident</h3>
  <p>
    Why insurers request photographs, reports, repair estimates, medical records, and other documentation, and how missing or delayed evidence can slow claim review.
  </p>
</a>
<a
  class="card"
  href="/resources/why-some-car-accident-claims-take-longer-than-others-california"
>
  <h3>Why some car accident claims take longer than others</h3>
  <p>
    Why claims can feel slow, including ongoing treatment, missing documentation, fault disputes, and how insurance review processes affect timing.
  </p>
</a>

<a
  class="card"
  href="/resources/why-is-my-car-accident-claim-taking-so-long-california"
>
  <h3>Why is my car accident claim taking so long?</h3>
  <p>
    Common reasons California car accident claims can feel slow, including ongoing treatment, missing records, fault disputes, insurance review, and multiple parties.
  </p>
</a>
<a
  class="card"
  href="/resources/can-pain-show-up-days-after-a-car-accident"
>
  <h3>Can pain show up days after a car accident?</h3>
  <p>
    Why soreness, headaches, neck pain, back discomfort, and other symptoms sometimes appear hours or days after a collision.
  </p>
</a>

<a
  class="card"
  href="/resources/why-some-car-accident-claims-stop-moving-forward-california"
>
  <h3>Why some car accident claims stop moving forward</h3>
  <p>
    Why insurance claims sometimes feel stuck, including communication slowdowns, documentation delays, internal review stages, and unresolved questions.
  </p>
</a>

```html
<a
  class="card"
  href="/resources/why-is-my-car-repair-taking-so-long-after-an-accident-california"
>
  <h3>Why is my car repair taking so long after an accident?</h3>
  <p>
    How inspections, hidden damage, supplemental estimates, parts delays,
    insurance review, body shop scheduling, and safety-system calibration can
    extend California collision repairs.
  </p>
</a>
```

        </div>

        <p style="margin-top: 1rem; opacity: 0.85;">
          More guides are coming soon. Start with the car accident checklist above.
        </p>
      </section>

    

      <section style="margin-top: 2.5rem; max-width: 75ch; opacity: 0.85;">
        <p style="margin:0;">
          <strong>Important:</strong> This website is an informational resource operated by a law student. 
          It is not a law firm and does not provide legal advice or legal representation. 
          Reading this site does not create an attorney–client relationship. 
          When appropriate, visitors may be referred to independent, licensed California attorneys. 
          No referral fees are accepted or paid.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
